+  // Optional filter that makes prepopulate_block_cache selective. When set,
+  // it is consulted once per data block that prepopulate_block_cache would
+  // warm, on the thread building the table, with the block's first and last
+  // internal keys; returning false leaves that block out of the cache. Meta
+  // blocks (index, filter) are never filtered. Only the synchronous write
+  // path is filtered: with parallel compression the keys of a block are not
+  // available at insertion time and every block is warmed as before.
+  //
+  // Added for Leaper (a learned prefetcher for cache invalidation): the
+  // prefetcher predicts which key ranges will be read after a flush or
+  // compaction and warms only the output blocks in those ranges, from
+  // memory, at the moment the builder produces them -- the paper's design.
+  std::shared_ptr<PrepopulateBlockFilter> prepopulate_block_filter;
